            Leaves out what sits at the top or bottom edge of the pages only because it is a page (running heads, footers,
            page numbers), so text exports read on without it:


paragraphs that repeat on most pages (digits are ignored, so "Page 3" matches "Page 4");

running heads that change with the chapter: the same text at the same height on three pages or more,
            no larger than the body text (a heading that starts several pages is larger, and stays);

bare page numbers ("12", "- 12 -", "Page 3 of 10", "iv");

the same picture (a logo) at the same place on most pages.
